{"id": "board-review-line-raised", "title": "Voters backed a higher threshold for Board review of City contracts", "seconds": 156.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "5ecd13548cc25bd8", "words": 443, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Since 1988, San Francisco has had a rule.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.03, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "pins": [{"place": "cityhall", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "votes on big contracts"}], "zoomOn": "board", "scale": 1.9, "kicker": "San Francisco, since 1988"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.66, 1.5, 1.73, 2.22, 2.35, 2.48, 2.54]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The spending threshold for nonconstruction contracts was 10 million dollars.", "t0": 3.15, "t1": 7.28, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "pins": [{"place": "cityhall", "name": "Board of Supervisors", "sub": "votes on big contracts"}], "zoomOn": "board", "scale": 1.9, "kicker": "San Francisco, since 1988"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.61, 1.12, 1.28, 1.99, 2.86, 3.11, 3.38, 3.68]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "It’s a check on how contractors perform, and how well the City keeps watch.", "t0": 7.4, "t1": 11.6, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "an opportunity to evaluate contractor performance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.25, 0.53, 0.63, 0.82, 1.43, 2.36, 2.55, 2.71, 3.03, 3.18, 3.46, 3.75]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[4]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "On November 3, voters considered a change.", "t0": 11.72, "t1": 15.76, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "sub": "November 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.96, 1.33, 2.02, 2.46, 2.99, 3.11]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "established[4]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "Proposition E would raise the spending threshold.", "t0": 15.76, "t1": 18.53, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Proposition E", "sub": "November 3, 2026"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.69, 1.24, 1.46, 1.78, 1.89, 2.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The new threshold would be 25 million dollars.", "t0": 18.65, "t1": 21.35, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$25 million", "label": "nonconstruction spending threshold after the effective date"}, "emph": ["25"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.37, 0.9, 1.05, 1.18, 1.84, 2.19]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "A term of ten years or more would also require Board approval.", "t0": 21.87, "t1": 24.85, "shot": "duration-rule", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "text": "Ten years or more", "mark": "Ten years or more", "kicker": "City Attorney · November 9"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 0.5, 0.72, 1.0, 1.14, 1.43, 1.61, 1.89, 2.33, 2.53]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[2]"], "text": "So what slips out of view?", "t0": 24.97, "t1": 27.25, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "the Board’s own research office"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.44, 0.76, 0.9, 0.98]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[2]"], "text": "The Board’s research office checked 2023 to 2025.", "t0": 27.25, "t1": 31.37, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Budget and Legislative Analyst", "sub": "the Board’s own research office"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.58, 0.99, 1.29, 1.59, 1.92, 2.81, 2.97, 3.31]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[6]"], "text": "About 2.5 billion dollars.", "t0": 31.49, "t1": 33.23, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$2.5 billion", "label": "would have skipped Board review, 2023 to 2025"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.45, 0.69, 0.95, 1.29]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[1]"], "text": "Proposition E would amend the City Charter.", "t0": 33.85, "t1": 35.97, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Three charter amendments", "sub": "proposed by Mayor Daniel Lurie, on the ballot by voter petition"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.63, 0.91, 1.08, 1.4, 1.52, 1.77]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[0]"], "text": "The earlier rule covered amendments with an impact over 500,000 dollars.", "t0": 36.09, "t1": 39.88, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Amendments", "sub": "The earlier and new approval rules"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.57, 0.84, 1.11, 1.48, 1.62, 1.71, 2.15, 2.39, 2.71, 2.99, 3.33]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[0]"], "text": "Under the new rule, an amendment first crossing a threshold needs a vote.", "t0": 40.0, "t1": 44.64, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Amendments", "sub": "The earlier and new approval rules"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.32, 0.51, 1.37, 1.53, 1.96, 2.55, 2.95, 3.02, 3.97, 4.24, 4.31]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "For a contract already approved under the new rules, accumulated increases can trigger review.", "t0": 44.76, "t1": 49.44, "shot": "limits", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "text": "50 percent of the original amount since the last Board approval", "mark": "50 percent of the original amount since the last Board approval", "kicker": "Amendments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.23, 0.71, 1.03, 1.48, 1.63, 1.73, 1.87, 2.64, 3.3, 3.79, 3.94, 4.25]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[10]"], "text": "The preliminary count showed 63.76 percent yes.", "t0": 49.56, "t1": 53.71, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["yes", "207,405"], "b": ["no", "117,874"], "mid": "Preliminary count · Firefighters Local 798 backed the measure"}, "emph": ["63.76 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.65, 1.12, 1.43, 1.95, 2.2, 2.47, 2.72, 3.59]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[11]", "story[3]"], "text": "Two committees named for the Mayor raised 13.07 million dollars.", "t0": 53.83, "t1": 58.03, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Raised by two committees named for the Mayor", "rows": [["Committee one", "$7,635,000"], ["Committee two", "$5,431,550"]]}, "emph": ["13.07 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.64, 0.85, 0.96, 1.08, 1.74, 2.06, 2.57, 2.83, 3.18, 3.45, 3.74]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[12]", "story[4]"], "text": "On November 10, the Mayor announced proposed purchasing legislation.", "t0": 58.15, "t1": 61.75, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A purchasing ethics chapter", "sub": "announced November 10, 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.53, 1.22, 1.38, 1.66, 2.01, 2.49, 2.98]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Now the leads. These are questions, not findings by any authority.", "t0": 61.97, "t1": 65.84, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Now, the leads", "sub": "not official findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.33, 1.5, 1.73, 1.88, 2.4, 2.59, 3.04, 3.2, 3.35]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Fewer contracts would qualify for review on spending alone.", "t0": 65.96, "t1": 69.09, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Spending threshold", "sub": "A separate rule covers contract length"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.4, 0.91, 1.08, 1.6, 1.75, 2.14, 2.28, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[6]"], "text": "The second lead: from 2023 to 2025, the Board reviewed 304 contracts.", "t0": 69.31, "t1": 75.75, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "304 contracts reviewed", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2023 to 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.52, 1.3, 1.5, 1.8, 2.42, 2.56, 2.83, 4.07, 4.2, 4.48, 4.9, 5.24, 5.59, 5.84]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[6]"], "text": "How many would have received spending review under the new rules?", "t0": 75.87, "t1": 79.6, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "304 contracts reviewed", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2023 to 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.35, 0.52, 0.64, 1.21, 1.58, 1.92, 2.1, 2.19, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[6]"], "text": "115.", "t0": 79.6, "t1": 80.69, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "115", "label": "contracts the analyst estimated would have required review", "sub": "189 fewer"}, "emph": ["115"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.51]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The analyst estimated that 189 fewer contracts would have received review.", "t0": 81.21, "t1": 86.68, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["fewer contracts reviewed", "189"], "b": ["annual spending in the estimate", "$830 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.6, 1.05, 1.25, 1.52, 1.91, 2.57, 3.06, 3.96, 4.18, 4.34, 4.97]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[7]"], "text": "The grand jury questioned what would replace that review.", "t0": 86.9, "t1": 89.7, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "No new oversight or audit mechanism is proposed in the amendments."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.49, 0.8, 1.27, 1.46, 1.66, 2.15, 2.33]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Departments would retain their own checks.", "t0": 89.82, "t1": 91.62, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Department oversight", "sub": "Spending threshold after the change: $25 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.43, 0.59, 0.96, 1.14, 1.31]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[8]"], "text": "The fourth lead: three times the Board’s review changed the outcome.", "t0": 91.84, "t1": 95.56, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Three times the vote mattered", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "Files 24-0994, 23-1247 and 23-0692"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.48, 1.2, 1.56, 1.99, 2.08, 2.36, 2.79, 3.15, 3.27]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "The Board cut one raise for the Mid-Market Foundation.", "t0": 95.68, "t1": 98.69, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mid-Market Foundation raise, asked", "$7.7 million"], "b": ["after Board review", "$3.8 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.58, 0.84, 1.13, 1.53, 1.65, 1.78, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "From 7.7 million dollars to 3.8 million.", "t0": 98.81, "t1": 102.58, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Mid-Market Foundation raise, asked", "$7.7 million"], "b": ["after Board review", "$3.8 million"]}, "emph": ["3.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.62, 0.91, 1.19, 1.47, 2.2, 2.38, 2.69, 3.02, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[2]"], "text": "For the Japanese Community Youth Council, the Board asked for an audit.", "t0": 102.7, "t1": 106.41, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "chip": "$5.6 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.25, 0.72, 1.16, 1.39, 2.19, 2.33, 2.72, 3.16, 3.29, 3.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[2]"], "text": "It found 5.6 million dollars paid without checking who qualified.", "t0": 106.53, "t1": 110.54, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Japanese Community Youth Council", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "chip": "$5.6 million"}, "emph": ["5.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.43, 0.72, 0.99, 1.34, 1.7, 2.03, 2.63, 2.96, 3.28, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Under the new lines, none of the three would have been heard.", "t0": 110.66, "t1": 113.09, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "None would be heard now", "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.29, 0.46, 0.98, 1.18, 1.25, 1.36, 1.65, 1.81, 1.91, 2.07]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "Under the change, the City Administrator could propose purchasing rules.", "t0": 113.31, "t1": 116.76, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City Administrator would propose purchasing rules", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "the City Administrator"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.34, 1.12, 1.25, 1.49, 2.09, 2.23, 2.63, 3.07]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The City Administrator, picked by the Mayor. How much spending do they cover each year?", "t0": 116.88, "t1": 122.02, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "City Administrator would propose purchasing rules", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "the City Administrator"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.33, 1.2, 1.44, 1.56, 1.66, 2.71, 2.9, 3.1, 3.53, 3.64, 3.77, 4.04, 4.21]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "established[3]"], "text": "More than 6 billion dollars.", "t0": 122.02, "t1": 123.72, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$6 billion", "label": "City contract spending a year"}, "emph": ["More"], "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.46, 0.85, 1.2]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[5]"], "text": "The Board would have 60 days to reject a proposal and could not amend it.", "t0": 124.24, "t1": 128.99, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Reject it whole, or not at all", "kicker": "The fifth lead", "sub": "60 days; no amendments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.55, 0.7, 0.87, 1.33, 1.79, 1.93, 2.26, 2.33, 3.3, 3.49, 3.69, 4.16, 4.55]}, {"scene": "record", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[13]"], "text": "The Board’s analyst had previously suggested lowering the threshold.", "t0": 129.21, "t1": 132.03, "shot": "record-13-2011", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ov11co", "text": "2011", "mark": "2011", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.88, 1.01, 1.5, 1.94, 2.25, 2.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show any contract has skipped review yet.", "t0": 132.25, "t1": 134.92, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any contract has skipped review yet", "That any donor holds a City contract"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.52, 0.74, 0.96, 1.13, 1.6, 1.73, 2.04, 2.36]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Or that any donor holds a City contract.", "t0": 135.04, "t1": 136.97, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any contract has skipped review yet", "That any donor holds a City contract"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.25, 0.45, 0.79, 1.13, 1.21, 1.44]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The certified results, due by December 3.", "t0": 137.09, "t1": 141.59, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Certified results, due by December 3, 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Contracts of $10 million to $25 million signed after the change"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.46, 0.79, 1.45, 1.64, 2.24, 3.29, 3.51, 3.66, 4.11]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "And a list of contracts in that range signed after the change.", "t0": 141.71, "t1": 144.57, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Certified results, due by December 3, 2026"}, {"who": "", "what": "Contracts of $10 million to $25 million signed after the change"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.2, 0.4, 0.5, 0.98, 1.08, 1.25, 1.6, 2.02, 2.24, 2.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["status", "established[14]"], "text": "The City Attorney expected the change in mid- to late December.", "t0": 144.69, "t1": 147.95, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "propEeffective", "text": "Expected in mid- to late December", "mark": "Expected in mid- to late December", "kicker": "City Attorney · November 9"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.41, 1.11, 1.66, 1.75, 2.11, 2.22, 2.44, 2.59, 2.8]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[14]"], "text": "First the Board declares the results. Then the Secretary of State must accept the filing.", "t0": 148.07, "t1": 153.08, "shot": "file-date", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "propEeffective", "text": "Board declaration and State acceptance", "mark": "Board declaration and State acceptance", "kicker": "City Attorney · November 9"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.73, 0.97, 1.38, 1.49, 2.64, 2.85, 2.95, 3.37, 3.45, 3.83, 4.07, 4.45, 4.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 153.2, "t1": 155.41, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.77, 0.92, 1.18, 1.24, 1.33, 1.55, 1.8]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · no vote", "lead2": "Lead 2 · 304 to 115", "lead3": "Lead 3 · nothing in its place", "lead4": "Lead 4 · three that mattered", "lead5": "Lead 5 · one office writes the rules", "close": "Where it stands", "record": "The public record"}, "look": "kinetic", "hook": "document"}